id: pm-b8hwfr
title: "Bun event streaming falls back to authoritative history without node:sqlite"
description: "Packed bunx --bun can initialize and mutate a workspace, but pm events fails with event_index_unavailable because Bun exposes no Node DatabaseSync constructor. Preserve SQLite acceleration on Node while adding a bounded authoritative history-stream fallback with filter, ordering, cursor, provenance, and limit parity so the universal event surface remains functional under Bun."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:sdk","github-pr:1053",mutation-events,"runtime:bun"
created_at: "2026-08-17T08:29:34.248Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T09:49:12.703Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T09:46:08.998Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T09:46:08.998Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-ez1dfg
resolution: "Authoritative Bun event fallback now caches ordered per-stream history with metadata invalidation and bounded root eviction, preserving filters/cursors while eliminating idle reparsing and resorting."
expected_result: "Repeated Bun follow polls reuse unchanged parsed streams; appends, rewrites, and deletes refresh only affected state without changing event ordering, pagination, or source receipts."
actual_result: "TDD regressions, 19 linked event tests, 58 focused remediation tests, typecheck, contract/surface gates, package artifact, secrets scan, defect evidence, and exact full 100/100/100/100 coverage pass."
fixed_version: unreleased
