comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T08:29:34.248Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-17: searched all statuses for Bun node:sqlite, bunx events, event_index_unavailable, and runtime compatibility. pm-cedo0g is the closed prior bundle-startup incident whose authoritative-read fallback covered the item metadata index but not the later history event index; this is its explicit recurrence for the new event surface. Reproduction: a locally packed 2026.8.17 tarball under bunx --bun successfully ran init and create, then pm events --cursor-mode batch returned event_index_unavailable."
  "2026-08-17T08:52:32.871Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the first focused run failed because queryHistoryEventStreams did not exist and listMutationEvents still threw event_index_unavailable. The implemented fallback now reads authoritative JSONL streams, preserves timestamp/stream/offset ordering, cursor and since bounds, operation/author/harness/instance/provenance/item filters, bounded limit plus has_more semantics, and reports source=authoritative_history. Focused PM test passes 17 tests; packed bunx --bun init/create/events acceptance returned a terminal batch cursor; full coverage passes 512 files and 7,469 tests at exact 100/100/100/100 (54,597 statements, 40,719 branches, 11,224 functions, 52,696 lines)."
  "2026-08-17T09:31:01.765Z","harness:codex","TDD review recurrence: focused tests first failed because unchanged authoritative streams were reparsed and NDJSON trailer counts were not validated. The cache test now proves unchanged entry identity, changed-stream refresh, deleted-stream invalidation, and bounded eight-root LRU eviction; ordered filtering no longer re-sorts idle polls."
  "2026-08-17T09:38:48.888Z","harness:codex","Full repository coverage after the cache recurrence: 512 covered files at exact 100/100/100/100 — 54,622/54,622 statements, 40,733/40,733 branches, 11,226/11,226 functions, and 52,720/52,720 lines. The focused five-file remediation suite passed 58/58 tests, including cache invalidation/LRU, mutation-event parity, NDJSON framing, SDK surface, and content-scoped replication governance."
  "2026-08-17T09:39:02.885Z","harness:codex","Coverage wording correction: the full Vitest run covers 512 test files; coverage-summary.json contains 602 covered source/report entries. The exact counters remain 54,622 statements, 40,733 branches, 11,226 functions, and 52,720 lines, all 100%."
  "2026-08-17T09:49:12.703Z","harness:codex","Post-close manual acceptance: a freshly packed tarball ran under bunx --bun in a temporary workspace, initialized and created an item, then emitted one authoritative_history event plus a valid pm.stream.trailer cursor. The full packed npx workflow also passed version/help, extension package install/catalog, calendar, upgrade, TypeScript consumer, and ./cli export checks (13 packages)."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-17T08:52:33.584Z","harness:codex","A rebuildable SQLite projection is an accelerator, not a portability prerequisite: every universal read surface needs an authoritative fallback with the same ordering, filtering, and pagination semantics plus a truthful source receipt."
  "2026-08-17T09:46:02.120Z","harness:codex","A portable authoritative fallback must cache at the stream boundary, not only preserve semantic parity: stat-signature invalidation lets idle follow polls avoid disk reads, JSON parsing, and sorting while append/rewrite/delete changes still rebuild the ordered aggregate deterministically."
